            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="CAM02" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName>Dr</roleName>
                        <forename>Thomas</forename>
                        <surname>Campbell</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1733-05-04">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1795-06-20"/>
                    <occupation>clergyman</occupation>
                    <occupation>traveller</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Campbell was a Church of Ireland clergyman who made a number of trips to London and recorded his observations in a diary. This diary records his thoughts on 
    Dr Johnson and his circle. He also published <title>Philosophical Survey of the South of Ireland in a Series of Letters to John Watkinson, MD</title> (1778) which 
  was intended to improve the image of Ireland in British eyes.</p>
                        <p>This identification is speculative. The two contacts are in 1790, the first referring to Dr Tho. Campbell; the second shortly aftyer with Brand Hollis.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
